Z||000000||Aussieken||01-18-2000||01:22 AM||||Does anyone have the front wheel alignments specs for an '88 model Formula ? Fieros are pretty rare down under. The wheel alignment guy thinks it's a spicy chicken dish from KFC.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phaeton||01-18-2000||02:50 AM||||All I have are factory specs and they give degrees instead of inches. Front toe is .3 degrees per wheel, camber is zero degrees.  If you are really doing it all caster is five degrees for formula and gt.  Its my rear end that gives me the most steering problems.  Rear toe is .15 degrees  per wheel and camber is minus one degree.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric||01-18-2000||05:11 PM||||Just so you know, I took all the negative camber out of the rear tires.  At first it seemed like the tires were wearing evenly and I did a good thing, but a few weeks ago and with 2,500 miles on the tires I noticed they were wearing in the middle.  My tire pressure has never gone above 32psi either.  So I'm going to put the camber back in because at this point it could only help matters.||||reg||1
